From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:34:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Name the bus node soc@0

With W=1, dtc reports unit_address_vs_reg for the "soc" node, which has a
ranges property but no unit address. Name it soc@0: its ranges map child
address 0 to parent address 0.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the bus node is soc@0 in
/proc/device-tree, and the devices probe under /soc@0/.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 69cff0d10ffb..31c6e7e023c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ timer {
 			     <GIC_PPI 10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 	};
 
-	soc {
+	soc@0 {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
